sbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JAPAN TOBACCO INC</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKODA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INABA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN TOBACCO INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKODA, KENJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INABA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKODA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INABA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKODA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Disubstituted maleimide compounds represented by general formula [I] or pharmaceutically acceptable salts thereof; and medicinal compositions and protein kinase (PKC)  beta -inhibitors containing these compounds. Because of selectively inhibiting PKC beta , these compounds are usable as efficacious and safe remedies and preventives for diseases caused by PKC such as complications of diabetes, wherein R&lt;1&gt; represents hydrogen or alkyl; R&lt;2&gt; represents aryl, cycloalkyl or a heterocycle; R&lt;3&gt;, R&lt;5&gt;, R&lt;6&gt;, R&lt;7&gt; and R&lt;8&gt; represent each hydrogen, halogeno, hydroxy, amino, alkyl or alkoxy; and R&lt;4&gt; is W, or R&lt;4&gt; and R&lt;3&gt; or R&lt;4&gt; and R&lt;5&gt; may form together a ring substituted by W thereon (wherein W represents -(CH2)1-(Y)m-(CH2)n-Z).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des composés de maléimide disubstitués représentés par la formule générale [I] suivante ou des sels pharmaceutiquement acceptables de ces derniers. L'invention a aussi pour objet des compositions médicinales et des inhibiteurs - beta  (PCK) de la protéine kinase contenant ces composés. Ces composés, qui inhibent la PKC beta  peuvent être utilisés comme produits thérapeutiques efficaces et sans danger et comme produits prophylactiques pour les maladies provoquées par la PKC, comme des complications du diabète. Dans la formule [I], R&lt;1&gt; représente hydrogène ou alkyle ; R&lt;2&gt; représente aryle, cycloalkyle ou un hétérocycle; R&lt;3&gt;, R&lt;5&gt;, R&lt;6&gt;, R&lt;7&gt; et R&lt;8&gt; représentent chacun hydrogène, halogéno, hydroxy, amino, alkyle ou alcoxy; et R&lt;4&gt; représente W ou R&lt;4&gt; et R&lt;3&gt; ou R&lt;4&gt; et R&lt;5&gt; peuvent former ensemble une chaîne substituée par W (où W représente -CH2)1-(Y)m-(CH2)n-Z).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms